From 4a0340eaf5617f2db79277c30dc5bc8136efe550 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mao, Roger" <roger.mao@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 23:11:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/13] Support VLA token + nav2_cmd dual-mode switching in
 ROS2 input handler

  Adds VLA-driven manipulation as a peer to navigate-driven locomotion in
  the same ROS2 input handler
    - Subscribe to ControlPolicy/vla_token (ByteMultiArray) carrying a
      ZMQ-Protocol-v4-compatible packed payload; parse 1280-byte JSON
      header + binary fields (token_state, toggle_vla_mode, frame_index,
      left/right_hand_joints)
    - Hand-joint payloads (shape [7] or [N,7], f32/f64) feed
      left_hand_joint_ / right_hand_joint_ via SetData(), matching ZMQ v4
      semantics so downstream GetHandPose() is transport-agnostic.
    - Fix toggle_policy_action 2nd-press behaviour: 1st pulse = START,
      2nd = PAUSE in place (planner stays enabled, navigate_cmd forced
      to 0, deploy does NOT exit)

Signed-off-by: Mao, Roger <roger.mao@intel.com>
---
